RMDIR(1)                     Funny CLI Manual                     RMDIR(1)

NAME
    rmdir — Remove a directory and everything inside it, because
    sometimes one file is simply not enough.

SYNOPSIS
    rmdir <dir>

DESCRIPTION
    The rmdir command removes the specified directory and all of its
    contents.

    Unlike the standard rmdir command, this version can remove
    non-empty directories.

USAGE
    > rmdir <dir>       # Removes the specified directory and its contents.

FUN FACTS
    - rmdir normally sounds harmless, but this version means business.
    - Everything inside the directory is removed recursively.
    - There is no recycle bin waiting to save you.
    - If the directory contains something important, you may want to
    think twice before pressing Enter.

EXAMPLES
    > rmdir documents
        Removes the documents directory and everything inside it.

    > rmdir /home/user/old_project
        Removes old_project and all of its contents.

    > rmdir missing
        Displays an error because the specified directory does not exist.

SEE ALSO
    help(1), ls(1), rm(1), cd(1), man(1)

    Remember, rmdir does not just close the door.
    It removes the entire house.

